# Inefficient mobile use

## User issue
The user finds the website difficult to use on mobile.

## Possible causes
- The design is not fully responsible.
- Buttons or interactive elements are too small.
- Content doesn’t fit on smaller screens.
- CSS media queries are missing or not working completely.

## Troubleshooting steps
1. Ask the user which device or browser they are using.
2. Ask them which part of the page or feature is difficult to use.
3. Test: Try to reproduce the issue on a similar device or screen size.
4. Check layout, responsiveness, and touch interactions.

## User-friendly response
Hi!

Thanks for reporting the issue; it is appreciated.

Could you let me know which device or browser you’re using, and which part feels difficult to use? That will help us investigate more accurately.

We will also check this on our side and get back to you. 

## Internal note
The issue might be related to responsiveness or a mobile UX issue. It could be layout problems, small interactive elements, or missing/incomplete media queries.



